  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Envelope 1: Provision of Shelter Support and Integrated Services for Vulnerable Populations in Northwest Syria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under this project, IOM proposes to provide dignified shelter, with complementary infrastructure, Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM), Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH), and Protection services in 12 informal sites and surrounding locations in Idleb, targeting 13,932 beneficiaries. In addition, IOM proposes to continue CCCM service provision in 10 IOM-managed Planned Camps (PCs) in Idleb and Aleppo to ensure the successful completion of the dignified shelter intervention under SCHF-funded project-20631. In total, 42,344 beneficiaries will be supported.</narrative>
  </description>
